// Single source of truth for the platform's India state → city taxonomy.
// Replaces the old flat ~7-city "metro only" lists that used to be hardcoded
// separately (and inconsistently) in three different frontend pages. See
// frontend/lib/locations.ts for the mirror.
//
// Selection is two-step: pick a state/UT, then pick one or more cities within
// it.
//
// As of 2026-09-18: 6,174 unique towns/cities across all 36 states and UTs
// (up from 3,845 on 2026-09-17, up from 1,801 before that). The base layer
// is every state's official urban local body roster (Municipal
// Corporations, Councils, Nagar Panchayats — Wikipedia's per-state "List of
// urban local bodies in X" / tehsil-list articles mirror state government
// gazette data). Layered on top of that: India's Census Towns — the
// Census of India's classification for populated places that meet urban
// criteria (density, non-agricultural workforce, population) but don't yet
// have a statutory municipal body — sourced from Census 2011 data via
// Wikipedia "List of census towns in X" articles/categories, individual
// settlement articles, and citypopulation.de's Census-derived tables,
// state by state. Per client feedback that the list should go as deep as a
// telecom coverage checker's — every town someone might actually live in,
// not just the well-known ones. It is still not literally every village in
// India (that's several hundred thousand more, with no clean bounded
// source — not attempted); if a specific town is still missing, add it
// here and mirror the same addition in frontend/lib/locations.ts.
// City values already stored on old records (all metro names) are preserved
// verbatim inside their correct state so legacy data keeps matching.

